 distance, and did not have the most hits at either 60 or 80 yards. Bryant had not previously won a national title, but won both individual events at the 1904 Olympics, and later won United States’ titles in 1905, 1909, and 1911-12. Silver medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/2255"} "Robert Williams"] " had won the US title in the Double York Round in 1883, 1885, and 1902, and is the only US Olympian known to have fought in the Civil War – he was 63 years old in 1904. Williams also won the silver in the " [:a {:href "/results/40511"} "Double American Round"] ". In fact, the podium in this event was the same as in the Double American Round, with Bryant winning gold, Williams winning silver, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2249"} "Will Thompson"] " taking the bronze. Williams and Thompson also led their Potomac Archers team to the gold medal in the " [:a {:href "/results/40515"} "Team Round"] ". This was the only time the Double York Round was contested at the Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Targets Hit"] [:th {} "Score"] [:th {} "100 y"] [:th {} "80 y"] [:th {} "60 y"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2225"} "Phil Bryant"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "7.0"] [:td {} "192"] [:td {} "820"] [:td {} "79 (1)"] [:td {} "67 (3)"] [:td {} "46 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2255"} "Robert Williams"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2.0"] [:td {} "191"] [:td {} "819"] [:td {} "78 (